# SilikOS: the installed GNOME Shell stylesheet's colours -> paper and ink, for every surface but the title bar and the
# lock and login screens (packages/silikos-desktop/files/shell-paper applies this; shell-theme.sed is their map).
# SOURCE -> TARGET; a source that ends with a comma maps every opacity of that colour. The sources are the shell's own
# dark theme (GNOME Shell 40): a colour that is not listed is left as it is.
# The paper family (silik-gtk3.css): paper #f7f6f3, paper2 #eeede9, field #fcfbf9, hover #e6e5e0, hairline #dcdad5,
# control border #8a8b8f, mid #b9b8b3, muted text #6b6d72, ink2 #2c2e32, ink #1a1b1e.
#
# text: the shell's light text -> ink; its greys -> ink2 (body text) and the muted grey (meta: 4.5:1 on paper and on
# the field); its text at 0.7 and 0.5 (hints, what is out of use) the muted grey too, the other opacities of that
# colour (lines, plates) ink at the same opacity; "white" is its brightest text on a dark surface, "#fff" its text on
# a chosen plate
#eeeeec -> #1a1b1e
#fafaf9 -> #1a1b1e
white -> #1a1b1e
rgba(238, 238, 236, 0.7) -> #6b6d72
rgba(238, 238, 236, 0.5) -> #6b6d72
rgba(238, 238, 236, -> rgba(26, 27, 30,
#e2e2df -> #2c2e32
#dbdbd6 -> #2c2e32
#d6d6d1 -> #2c2e32
#cacac4 -> #2c2e32
#c5c5be -> #6b6d72
#bebeb6 -> #6b6d72
#a6a69b -> #6b6d72
#878787 -> #6b6d72
#919190 -> #8a8b8f
#8e8e80 -> #8a8b8f
#fff -> #f7f6f3
#ffffff -> #f7f6f3
# what is selected, focused, on: the shell's accent blue and its tints -> ink (inverse video); the accents' own maps
# (accents/NAME.shell.sed, applied before this) give these sources their colours instead
#1b6acb -> #1a1b1e
#1c6fd4 -> #1a1b1e
#1d72d8 -> #2c2e32
#1f76e1 -> #2c2e32
#2c7fe3 -> #2c2e32
#1961b9 -> #1a1b1e
#1b68c6 -> #1a1b1e
#185fb4 -> #1a1b1e
#134c90 -> #1a1b1e
#092444 -> #1a1b1e
